01:02:27.166 --> 01:02:32.705
which is now, if
this technology is widely used,

01:02:32.706 --> 01:02:37.010
then the provider cannot have
learned some useful things

01:02:37.011 --> 01:02:39.485
like the route number five

01:02:39.486 --> 01:02:43.135
is hot or Thai
restaurant is popular.

01:02:43.136 --> 01:02:47.570
Have you thought about
any technology that still allows

01:02:47.571 --> 01:02:52.550
the provider to do
some statistical learning?

01:02:52.551 --> 01:02:56.165
Yeah. I think it's hard
within this model where

01:02:56.166 --> 01:03:00.130
its goal is kind of
hiding this information.

01:03:00.131 --> 01:03:01.240
If you have new information,

01:03:01.241 --> 01:03:04.395
it's hard to kind of do
some statistical learning.

01:03:04.396 --> 01:03:08.250
I think you can imagine
kind of a world where

01:03:08.251 --> 01:03:12.290
someone does these
aggregates independently.

01:03:12.291 --> 01:03:14.470
For example, like you know

01:03:14.471 --> 01:03:17.250
either anonymously or
where some third party

01:03:17.251 --> 01:03:19.180
does aggregation like using

01:03:19.181 --> 01:03:22.535
multiparty computation
or something like that.

01:03:22.536 --> 01:03:25.325
But I think that's
a separate problem,

01:03:25.326 --> 01:03:29.880
and you can't learn it from
the query directly like it's

01:03:29.881 --> 01:03:31.910
some separate system that's
kind of collecting a lot

01:03:31.911 --> 01:03:35.245
of this information and
kind of aggregating it.

01:03:35.246 --> 01:03:37.050
Yeah. And if you
care, we're trying to

01:03:37.051 --> 01:03:39.840
really prevent aggregates
from happening.

01:03:39.841 --> 01:03:42.305
But in the flight case,

01:03:42.306 --> 01:03:45.595
to the final purchase of ticket,

01:03:45.596 --> 01:03:48.170
that information
still can be used

01:03:48.171 --> 01:03:52.110
to do marketing or just a price.

01:03:52.111 --> 01:03:53.580
Yeah. In that case, it would be.

01:03:53.581 --> 01:03:54.970
But you kind of
prevent the problem

01:03:54.971 --> 01:03:56.390
where multiple people look

01:03:56.391 --> 01:03:57.870
for a certain flight and

01:03:57.871 --> 01:03:59.925
they raise the price
as a result.

01:03:59.926 --> 01:04:02.900
But if you purchase
a flight ticket, sure.

